-- Two-sided companion to showcase_observe_inequality: the observe predicate
-- confines the base to a bounded interval, so the set-valued witness engine
-- has to tighten one interval against another before meeting the query point.
-- Written as nested `if`s rather than `(v > 0.0) && (v < 1.0)` for historical
-- reasons only -- both spellings compile identically since task
-- set-witness-boolean-connectives; observeTwoSidedIntervalAnd is the `&&` twin
-- that pins the two agree value-for-value.
--
-- `p(Right ANY)` is then a CDF *difference*, Phi(1) - Phi(0), where the
-- one-sided program's is a single tail -- the case that distinguishes
-- "the wildcard drops the point constraint and keeps the interval" from
-- "the wildcard marginalises everything".
main = let v = Normal in if v > 0.0 then (if v < 1.0 then right v else left ()) else left ()
